-- ===========================================================================
-- IL-07 adapter for row IL-26: ITO s 164 and the Income Tax (Deduction from
-- Salary and Wages) Regulations 5753-1993, Schedule A.
--
-- VERSION 0.6.0 (2026-10-09, BACKLOG IL-55). Imports this row's nouns and row
-- IL-26's modules (vendored copies, VENDORED.sha256; its copies of row IL-03's
-- modules are the ones the capstone already vendors from row IL-03), and no other
-- row. FOR AN ENTRY POINT BESIDE THE PIPELINE: the capstone's answer is still one
-- twelfth of the year's tax (fork K1, reading (i)); this adapter gives the tax the
-- employer withholds from the month's salary (reading (ii)), which the pipeline
-- reports by its own name (fork K1, NOTES.md section 15).
--
-- INPUT CONVENTIONS (assumed, not ruled: the lead's direction for IL-55):
-- * the payment: the whole month's salary, paid in the tax year for which it is
--   paid, not a pension; a full-time position, as row IL-26's own standard payment
--   gives it: 22 days in the month, 8 hours a day, 40 a week (regulation 1 reads the
--   hours for a partial salary, five a day or fewer, and regulation 3 the days for
--   a day employee, fewer than 18); the pipeline asks this only of an earner to
--   whom the household says the full adult monthly minimum wage applies, and
--   declines any other, who may work part-time; the earner works nowhere else; a
--   foreign worker as the household says (row IL-26 declines one: Schedule C is not
--   encoded);
-- * the declarations: the employee's card given, with its section on other income
--   filled in (reg 5(a): otherwise the maximal rate) declaring none, and no
--   additional position; no form 0130; the credit points claimed are the points
--   the capstone composes for the tax year (the pipeline passes them);
-- * the figures: row IL-26's published annual figures for the tax year; the
--   readings: row IL-26's own switches; no direction of the assessing officer.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `IL-07 adapter — row IL-26`

@ref Regulations 5753-1993 regs 3, 5 and Schedule A (row IL-26, ito-il26-regulations.l4, `the withholding on`); the input conventions above
GIVEN h        IS AN `IL-07 household in a month`
      `points` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`IL-26: the tax withheld from the earner's salary for the month, in` h `, claiming` `points` `credit points` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the withholding on` `the payment` `given` `the declarations` `with` (`the annual figures published for tax year` `the year`)
                 `reading` `the readings of the withholding rules, by default` `under the direction` `no direction`
    WHEN RIGHT `the tax`  THEN `the tax`
    WHEN LEFT  `the problem` THEN `IL-26 reports that the facts cannot describe a payment of salary`
    WHERE
        e          MEANS h's `the earner`
        `the year` MEANS h's `the year of the month`
        `the payment` MEANS
            `A payment of salary` WITH
                `tax year`                                                                   IS `the year`
                `the tax year for which the salary is paid`                                  IS `the year`
                `the month's salary`                                                         IS e's `the earner's monthly salary`
                `the part of the month's salary paid in this payment`                        IS e's `the earner's monthly salary`
                `days worked in the month`                                                   IS 22
                `hours worked a day`                                                         IS 8
                `hours worked a week`                                                        IS 40
                `the payment is a pension`                                                   IS FALSE
                `the employee is a foreign worker`                                           IS e's `the earner is a foreign worker`
                `the employee works elsewhere, or receives a taxable pension from another payer` IS FALSE
        `the declarations` MEANS
            `The employee's declarations` WITH
                `gave the employer an employee's card (form 0101)`                                   IS TRUE
                `filled in the section of the card on other income`                                   IS TRUE
                `declared on the card an additional position, or a taxable pension from another payer` IS FALSE
                `declared on form 0130 that there is no other taxable income`                         IS FALSE
                `told the employer of other taxable income after making that declaration`             IS FALSE
                `credit points claimed on the card`                                                   IS `points`
                `date of birth`                                                                       IS e's `the earner's date of birth`

@ref Regulations 5753-1993 (row IL-26)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`IL-26 reports that the facts cannot describe a payment of salary` MEANS
    REFUSE "IL-26 reports that the facts cannot describe a payment of salary"
